## pi-permission-modes (schema reference and runtime imports)

- Source repository: https://github.com/wynainfo/pi-permission-modes
- License: MIT
- Copyright holder: Copyright (c) 2026 Nico Merz
- Version observed: 2.7.2, read from package.json of the package installed at
  `~/.pi/agent/npm/node_modules/pi-permission-modes` on 2026-11-26 (re-read that day, still 2.7.2; also 2.7.2 on 2026-11-25 and 2026-11-22). The
  version is observed, not pinned: nothing here fixes it, and the extension calls whatever is installed
  at run time. Version-drift risk: a different version may rename, remove or change the behavior of
  the imported functions, so re-read the installed version and re-check the names below when it
  changes. The referenced schema URL points at that repository's default branch (`main`) and is not
  pinned to this version.
- Where the content is used: runtime imports, not copies. `extensions/cwd-guard/index.ts` loads these
  files from the installed package, and `extensions/cwd-guard/rules.ts` receives the functions as
  arguments:
  - `src/bash-parse.ts`: `expandShellCommands`, `getTreeSitterParser`, `unwrapCommand`
  - `src/config-load.ts`: `loadModeConfig`
  - `src/heuristics.ts`: `normalizeBashToken`, `tokenTarget`
  - `src/paths.ts`: `insideRoots`, `isOutside`, `sandboxAllowedRoots`
  - `src/resolve.ts`: `mostRestrictive`, `resolveSurfaceDetailed`

  `src/schema.ts` is not imported: `rules.ts` declares the types it needs locally. Separately,
  `configs/permissions.example.src.jsonc:10` sets `$schema` to
  `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wynainfo/pi-permission-modes/main/schemas/permission-mode.schema.json`,
  and that value passes through unchanged into generated output, including
  `extensions/permission-mode-generator/sample.expected.json:2`.
- What was changed: nothing; no code or text from this source is copied or modified, and the schema URL
  is emitted as written. Any helper logic later vendored instead of called needs its own entry here.
- Originality: statements 1-3 of the cwd-guard prompt section come from the operator's earlier
  proof-of-concept at `~/.pi/agent/extensions/cwd-guard-poc/index.ts`. They are recorded here by
  reference to that path; no prompt body is copied into this record. Statement 4 and the reason text
  are original words written here, because the POC wording derives from `awareness.ts:270`.
